<spell-notebook "sidebar theming">
	<header level="1">
		Sidebar
		<header>A sidebar hides additional content beside a page.</>
	</>
	<sidebar-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-sidebar-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every
			sidebar), or on the box through `::part(sidebar)`.

			- The width words replace `--ui-sidebar-width`; `inverted` replaces `--ui-sidebar-background`.
			- `--ui-sidebar-duration`, `--ui-sidebar-dimmer-background` and `--ui-pusher-background` are read where they
			  paint (the sidebar, the pusher and its dimmer): set them on the pushable or any ancestor to reach them all, or
			  on the sidebar or the pusher alone.
			- `blurring` reads the shared dimmer tokens.
			- Style the boxes with `::part(pushable)` and `::part(pusher)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-sidebar {
			  --ui-sidebar-width: 300px;
			  --ui-sidebar-background: oklch(0.3 0.05 260);
			}
			ui-pusher::part(pusher) {
			  background: var(--ui-surface);
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				Never set the `--_ui-*` names (`--_ui-pusher-blurring` ...): they're the private switches the pushable sets on
				its pusher.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-sidebar" playground>
				<ui-pushable style="height: 14em">
					<ui-sidebar id="sidebar-demo-left-playground" inverted aria-label="Site">
						<ui-menu direction="vertical" inverted fluid aria-label="Site">
							<ui-item link="#home">Home</>
							<ui-item link="#games">Games</>
							<ui-item link="#channels">Channels</>
						</>
					</>
					<ui-pusher>
						<ui-segment appearance="basic">
							<button type="button" class="ui button" commandfor="sidebar-demo-left-playground" command="--toggle">Menu</>
							<ui-text paragraph>The default left sidebar uncovers itself from under this content, which dims.</>
						</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>The theme menu in the header (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) restyles the menu inside a sidebar.</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
